comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:08:17.895Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for stateless MCP server/discover request metadata protocolVersion clientCapabilities serverInfo resultType initialize removal and unsupported version handling. Existing handshake work is terminal and targets 2025-06-18."
  "2026-08-25T14:41:15.407Z","harness:codex","Evidence: public typed SDK protocol contracts, stateless per-request validation, deterministic server/discover, complete result envelopes, identity metadata, unsupported-version and missing-capability errors, legacy adapter, and real stdio coverage are implemented. Final exact-tree coverage: 574 files, 7920 tests, statements 57964/57964, branches 43503/43503, functions 12075/12075, lines 55865/55865. PM-linked typecheck, coverage, complete-tracker static assurance, and 49-test MCP cohort passed."
  "2026-08-25T15:01:37.533Z","harness:codex","Superseding final-tree evidence after legacy _meta era-selection fix: PM-linked full suite passed all four links. Exact coverage: 574 files, 7921 tests, statements 57964/57964, branches 43505/43505, functions 12075/12075, lines 55865/55865. Focused SDK/direct-handler/real-stdio cohort: 50 tests passed. Complete-tracker static assurance passed with persisted tracker context."
  "2026-08-25T15:29:06.260Z","harness:codex","Final frozen-source evidence after envelope integrity review: PM-linked exact coverage passed with 574 files and 7921 tests; statements 57971/57971, branches 43511/43511, functions 12077/12077, lines 55872/55872. Modern tool execution errors now retain resultType complete and serverInfo metadata, protocol errors remain JSON-RPC errors, and method-specific result metadata is preserved."
  "2026-08-25T15:48:20.816Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence: DeepScan reported high-severity NULL_POINTER 233240748 in src/mcp/server.ts because the modern dispatcher parameter was cast from possibly absent request metadata. Replaced the cast with an isModernMcpRequest TypeScript type predicate so request.params._meta is structurally proven before dispatch. Exact verification on the remediated source: focused MCP suite 13/13 passed; ESLint passed; Prettier passed; typecheck passed; full coverage passed 574 files and 7,921 tests with 100% statements (57,970/57,970), branches (43,511/43,511), functions (12,077/12,077), and lines (55,871/55,871). The complete static suite passed every functional and governance assertion through SDK entrypoint costs; its final local timing-only transport-floor probe exceeded ceilings under sustained host load (load average above 7), while the PR's hosted Gates (static) is the authoritative uncontended check."
  "2026-08-25T16:01:33.902Z","harness:codex","Final pre-close review evidence on the review-hardened source: CodeRabbit's three actionable findings were addressed through PM lifecycle reconstruction, Array.isArray discovery validation in release/Codex/Claude probes with scalar negative fixtures, and explicit protocol-version-key routing before legacy initialize with invalid-type and modern-initialize negative tests. Focused cohort passed 59/59; typecheck, lint, formatting, and changelog checks passed; exact coverage passed 574 files and 7,923 tests with statements 57,970/57,970, branches 43,514/43,514, functions 12,077/12,077, and lines 55,874/55,874."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T14:41:16.143Z","harness:codex",Linked repository assurance commands that inspect the governed tracker must declare pm_context_mode=tracker; the default schema context intentionally has zero real items and can produce a contextually false defect-evidence failure.
  "2026-08-25T14:41:16.933Z","harness:codex","Unversioned requests cannot prove modern protocol intent, so compatibility must classify them as legacy; strict 2026-07-28 metadata validation begins only when that version is explicitly claimed."
